  "body": "The existing incoming card identifies six emitted `shx.core` calls whose runtime is absent. This planning refinement proposes a complete, isolated runtime and its observable contracts while preserving the original choice to implement the runtime or narrow the emitter's claimed support. Native planning review must adjudicate that preference, semantics, and the existing five-point estimate before implementation.\n\nThe proposal covers all six symbols, portable law/shape/domain decisions and outer host adapters, explicit generated imports and run lifecycle, environment/PATH/alias propagation to exec/pipe/capture/raw branches, isolated Bash source deltas, and test true/false/error semantics. Positive and hostile generated-script fixtures must prove parent/run isolation and nonzero generated-script plus official test-runner failures. All seven `bin/analyze --strict` gates and mutation obligations for changed pure layers remain required.\n\nThis is an eight-path planning/evidence change stacked on sync PR1's exact branch `codex/shx-sync-upstream-f4ee133` at `f4ee133dcf1650c7eafb623ef084f62417252477`. The original card's complete 652-byte prefix, UUID, incoming/P1/five-point frontmatter, event ledger and all unrelated source/configuration remain intact. The receipt prefix is byte-exact; the reflection ledger is new because the base has no reflection file. Existing [PR2](https://github.com/riatzukiza/shx/pull/2) retains its emitted-string, CLI and Bash-test/mutation scope; no branch is adopted and no overlapping implementation is authorized.\n\nPreparation: the first private full gate exited 1 because copying the npm cache dereferenced an internal jscpd executable link. That failure is preserved. A distinct run after repairing only private internal links completed all seven checks, with 19 tests / 46 assertions on unchanged accepted source. The inherited typed.clojure deprecation remains visible. The actual current Receipt River owner at `154440f3c997aa9208194bba59b5edbef3654f78` admits only the three new declared rows 58\u201360 at this head; historical river validity is not claimed. Source preservation, strict 24-stream integrity and independent peer checks passed. These are preparation results, not future runtime or hosted qualification.\n\nDesign: `docs/notes/shx-core-runtime-plan.md`; original-card refinement: `kanban/shx-core-runtime-missing.md`; immutable preparation transports and preservation proof: `.\u03b7\u03bc/verification/shx-core-runtime-planning/`.\n\nCurrent head: `e271747deae46bd2f50d77d3a7b8d4b8f0d4ca00`. Ready PR, blocked, automatic merge off. Sync PR1 remains separately unqualified. Native planning qualification, reviewed decisions/size and a lawful Rheos ready transition precede implementation. No code, new runtime tests, board transition, manual reviewer request, settings, merge or deployment is part of this publication.\n",
